# Elisha Bay — Apache config for the project root.
#
# The project now lives inside the web root, which means anything in the
# folder is reachable over HTTP unless it is refused here. These rules block
# the things that are on disk for the developer's benefit, not the visitor's.

# 1. Editor/tooling config and archived source. .claude and .agents hold skill
#    definitions, and _archive holds the pre-RBAC source zip — none of it
#    should be downloadable.
RedirectMatch 404 (?i)/\.(claude|agents|mcp\.json)
RedirectMatch 404 (?i)/_archive/
RedirectMatch 404 (?i)/skills-lock\.json

# 2. SQL. schema.sql and seed.sql carry the table layout and, until Phase 2
#    hashes them, credentials.
RedirectMatch 404 (?i)/db/.*\.sql$

# 3. Internal docs and tooling.
RedirectMatch 404 (?i)/docs/
RedirectMatch 404 (?i)/tools/(?!ui-test/)

#    tools/ui-test/ is the exception: it is a test page that has to be OPENED
#    in a browser, so a blanket 404 would make it useless. It carries the
#    seeded test-account passwords, so it is restricted to the local machine
#    by tools/ui-test/.htaccess. It must not be reachable from anywhere else,
#    and it should not ship. (<Directory> is a server-config directive and
#    causes a 500 in .htaccess, hence the child file.)

# 4. Config. These files execute rather than being served as source while
#    mod_php is active, so this is defence for the case where it is not —
#    a disabled PHP module would otherwise hand out the DB password.
RedirectMatch 404 (?i)/api/config/

# 5. Development caching.
#    Browsers hold on to .js and .css aggressively, which during development
#    means editing a file and testing the previous version without realising
#    it — an easy hour to lose chasing a bug that is already fixed on disk.
#    Remove this block (or swap it for a long max-age) before deploying
#    anywhere real; caching is desirable then, and cache-busting should move
#    to versioned filenames.
#    HTML is included deliberately. Changing the <script> tags in a portal page
#    and then testing the cached previous version produced errors that looked
#    like a broken module conversion but were a stale document — twice. The
#    page is small; revalidating it costs nothing in development.
<FilesMatch "\.(js|css|html)$">
    Header set Cache-Control "no-cache, must-revalidate"
</FilesMatch>

# 6. Directory listings stay off everywhere.
Options -Indexes

# 7. Land on the storefront rather than a listing.
DirectoryIndex index.html index.php
